Make XRogue's state handling portable and keep it in ROGUEHOME.

Upstream stores 32-bit integers in score and save files, but its long and
unsigned long readers read those four bytes into an uninitialised 8-byte host
long on LP64 systems, so the upper bytes of every score are garbage.  Read and
write exactly 32 bits and widen or narrow them explicitly.

rogue.h declares d_list and f_list as arrays of a structure that is only
defined in daemon.c and state.c; declare them where the type is complete.

Let an explicit ROGUEHOME govern saved games as well as the score file, and
refuse a ROGUEHOME (or home directory) whose save and score file names would
not fit in their LINELEN buffers instead of overflowing or truncating them,
and keep the message line within its buffer when a prompt names such a path.
md_getroguedir copied ROGUEHOME with a PATH_MAX bound into a 1024-byte buffer,
which strncpy padding overruns on every call; copy only a directory that fits
the buffer together with the score file suffix.
Guard all three passwd lookups against a missing entry, and open the score
file read-only for "xrogue -s" so that listing scores never creates or
rewrites it and works when the file is not writable.

